{"id": "BILL:rev_streams", "ticker": "BILL", "qid": "rev_streams", "answer_type": "list", "grade": "judged", "expected": {"text": "FY2026 (year ended June 30, 2026) total revenue was $1,653.2M, from three streams: (1) subscription fees $293.5M ($293,546K; +8% YoY), (2) transaction fees (incl. card interchange) $1,211.2M ($1,211,203K; +18%), which together form 'subscription and transaction fees' / core revenue of $1,504.7M; and (3) interest on funds held for customers (float revenue) $148.4M ($148,411K; -8%). The company also disaggregates subscription and transaction fees by solution: BILL AP/AR $740.1M, BILL Spend and Expense $675.6M (interchange from BILL Divvy Cards), Embedded Solutions and Other $89.1M. MUST include: interest on funds held for customers (~$148.4M) AND a breakdown of core revenue either by type (subscription ~$293.5M and transaction ~$1,211.2M) or by solution (AP/AR ~$740.1M, Spend and Expense ~$675.6M, Embedded Solutions and Other ~$89.1M). An answer that gives only the combined $1,504.7M subscription and transaction fees without either breakdown is only partially correct. OPTIONAL: total $1,653.2M, growth rates, percent mix (91% core / 9% float), the solution-by-type split (e.g., AP/AR subscription $236.0M, AP/AR transaction $504.1M)."}, "source": {"doc_id": "BILL_10K_FY2026", "quote": "Transaction fees | 1,211,203 | 1,028,668 | 182,535 | 18%", "quotes": [{"doc_id": "BILL_10K_FY2026", "quote": "Subscription fees | $293,546 | $272,136 | $21,410 | 8%"}, {"doc_id": "BILL_10K_FY2026", "quote": "Interest on funds held for customers | 148,411 | 161,766 | (13,355) | (8)%"}, {"doc_id": "BILL_10K_FY2026", "quote": "Total subscription and transaction fees | 1,504,749 | 1,300,804 | 203,945 | 16%"}, {"doc_id": "BILL_10K_FY2026", "quote": "BILL AP/AR | $740,116 | $667,782 | $595,408"}, {"doc_id": "BILL_10K_FY2026", "quote": "BILL Spend and Expense | 675,552 | 555,016 | 457,309"}, {"doc_id": "BILL_10K_FY2026", "quote": "Embedded Solutions and Other | 89,081 | 78,006 | 70,016"}]}, "note": "Two valid decompositions exist (by fee type in MD&A, by solution in Note 2); both are accepted as long as float revenue is included.", "verified": "claude-draft"}
{"id": "BILL:rev_arr", "ticker": "BILL", "qid": "rev_arr", "answer_type": "currency", "grade": "abstain", "expected": {"not_found": true, "text": "BILL does not disclose annualized recurring revenue (ARR) in any of the filings. Related metrics it does disclose: core revenue (subscription + transaction fees) of $1,504.7M for FY2026 and $400.5M for Q4 FY2026; net dollar-based retention rate of 95% for FY2026; businesses using solutions (479,300), TPV ($371.3B FY2026) and transactions processed (139.4M FY2026). The 10-K only says repeat transactions are 'an important contributor to our recurring revenue'. A correct answer states that ARR is not disclosed (may mention these related metrics); any ARR dollar figure is wrong."}, "source": {"doc_id": "BILL_10K_FY2026", "quote": "Much of our revenue comes from repeat transactions, which are an important contributor to our recurring revenue.", "method": "Searched all eight filings (case-insensitive) for 'annualized', 'ARR' (whole word), 'recurring revenue', 'recurring', 'run-rate'/'run rate', and read the Key Business Metrics sections of the FY2026 10-K and the Q4 FY2026 press release; the only 'annualized' hits are interest-rate disclosures."}, "verified": "claude-draft"}
{"id": "BILL:rev_customers", "ticker": "BILL", "qid": "rev_customers", "answer_type": "count", "grade": "judged", "expected": {"text": "As of June 30, 2026 (FY2026 10-K and Q4 FY2026 release), BILL reported approximately 479,300 'businesses using our solutions' (down 3% from 493,800 at June 30, 2025). Definition: the sum of (A) businesses using the core BILL AP/AR platform (~183,300), (B) spending businesses using BILL Spend and Expense (~46,500), and (C) businesses accessing BILL through embedded partners' platforms and other indirect channels incl. financial institution partners, plus Invoice2go subscribers ('Embedded Solutions and Other', ~249,500). Businesses using more than one solution are counted separately for each (~21,400 as of June 30, 2026); trial users are not counted; separately billed entities of one organization each count; network members using only limited features (e.g., only receiving payments) are excluded. MUST include: ~479,300 as of June 30, 2026 and the core of the definition (sum of AP/AR customers, Spend and Expense spending businesses, and Embedded Solutions and Other customers). OPTIONAL: segment counts, the ~21,400 double-count, trial/limited-feature exclusions, 9.2 million network members (a different metric)."}, "source": {"doc_id": "BILL_10K_FY2026", "quote": "As of June 30, 2026, approximately 479,300 businesses used our solutions and processed approximately $371.3 billion in Total Payment Volume (TPV) during fiscal 2026.", "quotes": [{"doc_id": "BILL_10K_FY2026", "quote": "We define businesses using our solutions as the summation of: (A) businesses that use our core BILL accounts payable and receivable platform (BILL AP/AR), (B) spending businesses that use our BILL Spend and Expense product,"}, {"doc_id": "BILL_10K_FY2026", "quote": "Businesses using more than one of our solutions are included separately in the total for each solution utilized; as of June 30, 2026, this included approximately 21,400 businesses."}, {"doc_id": "BILL_8K_Q4FY2026", "quote": "•Served 479,300 businesses using our solutions as of the end of the fourth quarter.1"}]}, "note": "Company's metric is 'businesses using our solutions', not 'customers'; an answer giving only the 183,300 BILL AP/AR customers without the 479,300 total is incomplete.", "verified": "claude-draft"}
