{"id": "BOX:restructuring", "ticker": "BOX", "qid": "restructuring", "answer_type": "text", "grade": "judged", "expected": {"text": "Yes. During fiscal 2026 Box conducted a workforce reorganization to better align resources with strategic priorities, recording charges of approximately $10.6 million ($10,629 thousand) for the year ended January 31, 2026, primarily severance and termination benefits, continued employee health benefits and other personnel costs (most of it, ~$8.2 million, in the first half of FY2026). The headcount impact (number or percentage of employees affected) is not disclosed; total headcount still rose to 2,912 at Jan 31, 2026 from 2,810. MUST: yes, ~$10.6 million total charge, and that the headcount reduction is not disclosed. An answer inventing a headcount figure is wrong."}, "source": {"doc_id": "BOX_10K_FY2026", "quote": "During fiscal year 2026, we conducted a workforce reorganization effort to better align our resources with our strategic priorities. This resulted in charges of approximately $10.6 million for the year ended January 31, 2026,", "quotes": [{"doc_id": "BOX_10K_FY2026", "quote": "Workforce reorganization | 10,629 | 0.9 | — | — | 912 | —"}, {"doc_id": "BOX_10Q_Q2FY2026", "quote": "This resulted in charges of approximately $1.1 million and $8.2 million for the three and six months ended July 31, 2025, respectively,"}]}, "verified": "claude-draft", "note": "Searched 'workforce reorganization', 'restructuring', 'reduction in force', 'headcount reduction', 'employees impacted' across all filings; no affected-employee count is disclosed."}
